  "id": "paradigm-shift",
  "term": "paradigm shift",
  "definition": "A paradigm shift is a fundamental change in the basic framework used to understand and guide a field. In this context, it describes the move in mental health law from a biomedical model toward a human rights-based approach that changes assumptions about coercion, decision-making, and participation.",
